RETAIN COMPARISON, STORAGE AND RECOVERY BOUNDARIES
The comparator requires independently selected C/genesis and two complete accepted
ChainV2 values. Checks current C/genesis then candidate C/genesis. Same literal
fixed target means height 0..4095 is normalized work ordering; no work total is
multiplied. Higher candidate wins; ties keep current, with no global tie winner.
Hash magnitude, timestamps, population, money and local generation add no score.
Actual matching header hashes establish common ancestry; equal balances/state roots
do not. It compares at most 4,096 accepted pairs / 8,192 header hashes without allocations
or replay, and returns a private immutable whole-chain borrow. Finite caps/terminal
timestamps may prevent tie resolution. This is not final human consensus.

StoreV2 profile 1 keeps exact 232-byte MSS2/generation 0. AppendStoreV2 profile 2 keeps
exact 280-byte MSU2 and unchanged nested MSS2. Independent full checkpoint/generation
pins remain mandatory. Normal opening fully replays selected history and rejects
staging. Both implemented stores use cooperative Linux root-directory inode locks:
exclusive writers/shared inspectors. Trusted parent/local owner; never replace,
rename or remove a locked root, infer ownership from PID files, or claim same-user
hostile-race protection. Inherited fork descriptors can prolong locks; preserve
process-test isolation. WSL/DrvFS/native Windows/network mounts remain unverified.

Append validates the whole child, rechecks selected history, syncs block/directory,
prepares/syncs selector, checks old selection, renames marker and syncs root before
memory advances. Errors fence normal state access and writes. last_confirmed_checkpoint
means prior confirmed memory only. Clean reopen/reconcile fully replay and resync;
consuming reconciliation retains the same lock. It repairs no staging.

Explicit append recovery independently pins parent/candidate adjacent checkpoints
and exact child. It fully replays parent and accepts child before Complete or
RetainParent. It changes only authorized matching prefixes/paths. A pending selector
requires complete child; selected candidate requires clean complete history and
supports only idempotent Complete, never RetainParent rollback. Unknown/corrupt
selected bytes, unsafe aliases and initialization failures stay preserved/rejected.
Prefix equality does not prove origin; independent request supplies authority.
Consuming recovery retains ownership; every error returns no usable handle. Final
strict replay/equality/resync precedes success. No journal/automatic repair exists.
Its distinct encoded input cap 19,559,412 bytes and conservative payload-read allowance
156,508,096 bytes remain separate from RSS. One-child recovery is not generic reorg.

